 \u8212 ?it makes sick people sicker. And thus, this way of providing a remedy for pain, measured by modern standards, is a \uc1 \u8220 ?guilty\uc1 \u8221 ? method. However, to be fair, we must insist all the more that it was used}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  in good conscience}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 , that the ascetic priest prescribed it with the deepest faith in its utility, indeed, its indispensability\uc1 \u8212 ?often enough almost falling apart himself when in front of the misery he created; and, similarly, that the vehement physiological revenges of such excesses, perhaps even psychic disturbances, basically do not really contradict the whole meaning of this kind of medication, which, as I\uc1 \u8217 ?ve pointed out above, was }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 not }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 designed to heal sick people, but to fight their enervating depression, to alleviate and anaesthetize it.\uc1 \u160 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 With this method\uc1 \u160 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 that goal was attained. The main instrumental fingering which the ascetic priest allowed himself in order to bring every kind of disorienting ecstatic music ringing out in the human soul was achieved, as everyone knows, by the fact that he made use of the}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  feeling of guilt}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 . The previous essay indicated, in brief, the origin of this feeling\uc1 \u8212 ?as a part of animal psychology, nothing more. The feeling of guilt we encountered there in its raw state, as it were. In the hands of the priest, this true artist in guilt feelings, it first acquired a form\uc1 \u8212 ?and what a form! \uc1 \u8220 ?Sin\uc1 \u8221 ?\uc1 \u8212 ?for that\uc1 \u8217 ?s how the priest\uc1 \u8217 ?s new interpretation of the animal \uc1 \u8220 ?bad conscience\uc1 \u8221 ? ran (cruelty turned backwards)\uc1 \u8212 ?has been the greatest event in the history of the sick soul so far. In it we have the most dangerous and the most fateful artistic work of religious interpretation. The human being, suffering from himself somehow\uc1 \u8212 ?at any rate, psychologically\uc1 \u8212 ?something like an animal barred up in a cage, confused about why this has happened and what purpose it serves, longing for reasons\uc1 \u8212 ?reasons provide relief\uc1 \u8212 ?longing also for treatments and narcotics, finally discussed the matter with a one who also knew about hidden things\uc1 \u8212 ?and lo and behold! He gets a hint. He gets the}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  first\uc1 \u160 ? }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 hint about the \uc1 \u8220 ?cause\uc1 \u8221 ? of his suffering from his magician, the ascetic priest. He is to seek this cause in}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  himself}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 , in\uc1 \u160 ?his }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 guilt}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 , in a piece of the past. He is to understand his\uc1 \u160 ?own suffering as a\uc1 \u160 ?condition of punishment ... He heard, he understood\uc1 \u8212 ?this unfortunate man: now things stand with him as with a hen around which a line has been drawn. He is not to come outside this circle of lines again. The \uc1 \u8220 ?sick man\uc1 \u8221 ? is turned into the \uc1 \u8220 ?sinner\uc1 \u8221 ?... And now for a couple of millennia people have not rid themselves of the look of this new sick man, the \uc1 \u8220 ?sinner.\uc1 \u8221 ?\uc1 \u8212 ?Will people ever be rid of him?\uc1 \u8212 ?No matter where we look, we see everywhere the hypnotic glance of the sinner, who always moves in one direction (in the direction of \uc1 \u8220 ?guilt\uc1 \u8221 ? as the }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 single }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 cause of suffering), everywhere the bad conscience, this \uc1 \u8220 ?horrifying animal,\uc1 \u8221 ? to use Luther\uc1 \u8217 ?s words, everywhere the past regu