ch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs20 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs15 \fs20 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \super1 \chftn }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af5 \afs20 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs20 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Lev Tolstoy (1828\uc1 \u8211 ?1910), Russian realistic novelist who, in response to the pathologies of modernity, championed an agrarian Christian utopianism.}}}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \f5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  But so far as that other style of historian is concerned, maybe an even \uc1 \u8220 ?more modern\uc1 \u8221 ? style, which is comfortable and sensual and makes eyes at life as much at the ascetic ideal\uc1 \u8212 ?this style uses the word \uc1 \u8220 ?artist\uc1 \u8221 ? as a glove and has taken an exclusive lease on the praise of contemplation. O what a thirst these sweet and witty types arouse in people even for ascetics and winter landscapes! No! Let the devil take these \uc1 \u8220 ?meditative\uc1 \u8221 ? people! I would much prefer to keep wandering with those historical nihilists through the gloomiest cold grey fog!\uc1 \u8212 ?In fact, if I had to choose, I might find it better to lend an ear to a completely and essentially unhistorical or anti-historical man (like that D\uc1 \u252 ?hring, whose tones intoxicate a species of \uc1 \u8220 ?beautiful souls\uc1 \u8221 ? in Germany today,}{\cs15 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \super1 \chftn {\footnote \pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \sa60 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \tql \tx1200 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang102